v1.3.12 (2026-05-28)
--------------------
Fix: DHCP leases and NAT sessions not shown in hub NAT/DHCP tab.

Two bugs:

1. Indication — backend read "Log" key from EnumNAT/EnumDHCP response but
   SoftEther JSON-RPC returns "NatTable" / "DhcpTable". Affected all servers,
   even direct RPC — sessions were always empty regardless of actual activity.

2. Detection — EnumNAT and EnumDHCP had no vpncmd fallback implementation.
   VPN Azure (NAT-T) servers always returned empty arrays silently.
   Fixed by implementing NatTable / DhcpTable vpncmd commands with column
   mapping confirmed from SoftEther source (Command.c PsNatTable/PsDhcpTable).

3. MAC address in DHCP leases displayed as raw base64 (e.g. "yrtzAoQL")
   instead of AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF — fixed by calling _macBinToHex() in the
   DHCP leases table render (same function already used elsewhere).

Note: hostname column shows only if client included DHCP option 12 in its
request — expected behaviour, not a bug.
